**Hard rule:** never hardcode `/root/...` paths in skill scripts/tests. Use `Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent`.

**Wrong:**
```python
SKILL_DIR = Path("/root/.hermes/profiles/fst-control/skills/productivity/fst-project-health")
```

**Right:**
```python
SKILL_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
```

**Why:** user must be able to `tar czf skill.tar.gz <skill>/`, copy to another server, untar, and have everything work without modification. Verified by simulating copy to `/tmp/test-portability/` — both `tests/run_all_tests.py` and pipeline work from the new location.

**Files to patch:** every `SKILL_DIR = Path("/root/...")` in `scripts/*.py` and `tests/*.py`. Use `sed -i 's|SKILL_DIR = Path("/root/...|SKILL_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent|'`.

**Also applies to:** `mcp_config.py` `ENV_FILE = Path.home() / ".hermes/profiles/fst-control/.env"` — this is FINE (uses `Path.home()`), but the dirname `.hermes/profiles/fst-control/` may not match on another server. Document the env var convention; don't rely on a specific profile name.

